{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments","id":1503456,"title":"Home brew merits vs Arcane attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-19T09:18:28-08:00","id":1503456,"title":"Home brew merits vs Arcane attainments","content":"Something i was reading about a 1.5e homebrew got me thinking about custom magic 'styles' which could be added (or removed) from the game.<br /> <br /> Throw spell could have been a supernatural merit, and a pre-requisite for fast spells.<br /> <br /> Counter spell, likewise<br /> <br /> Or a Highspeech, Runic writing, Second Person High Speech, Invisible runes series of merits...<br /> <br /> I'd like some alternatives to the Order specific merits. Maybe an Oneiromacy series starting with Astral Adept?<br /> <br /> What are the relevant advantages of custom merits over custom Arcane attainments/alternative utility attainments? / Legacies?<br /> <br /> I think i want something like a set of minor legacy 'skill trees' which don't lock you out of other learning (With or without Arcana pre-reqs)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T10:28:42-08:00","id":1503458,"title":"","content":"Legacy Attainments have one huge selling point: consistency. You can be in an Abyssal Verge where time is inconsistent and your Legacy's time travel and divination Attainments will work fine whereas everyone else has a terrible time. You could be in an Ansho and your Legacy's physical enhancements will remain steady, the spells under your <i>Hung Spell</i> Attainment ready to go and your <i>Co-Location</i> Attainment connecting to the Sanctum still available. They cannot be counterspelled, Dissonanced away or effected by the Lie, they are always there when you need them.<br /> <br /> Utility Attainments are something that I imagine is rarer, you would need to quest to an ancient ruin, the depths of a Realm Invisible or complete some kind of great work to learn one beyond the ones in the core book. They make a major difference in your toolkit and should be considered a rare and precious prize.<br /> <br /> Style merits are just a body of knowledge that has been refined and codified into teachable skills. They should be easier to learn, should you find a teacher or reference containing them. But they are subject to being manipulated like anything else, such as a Prelate of Fury instinctively countering combat styles in just the right way.<br /> <br /> Overall, I recommend not giving out spells themselves in these skill trees, but rather supernatural moves that can help specialize your approach. Try looking at how <i>Hurt Locker</i> specializes combat styles and try to translate the spirit of it into these styles, I did something along those lines when making a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1486552-adamant-hand-fighting-style\">fighting style version of the Adamant Hand</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T11:25:39-08:00","id":1503464,"title":"","content":"The advantage of custom Merits is that Merits are the design space the game has set aside for &quot;use this space for any mechanical widget that you're not building a whole new subsystem or powerset for.&quot;<br /> <br /> Arcanum Attainments aren't framed as something for which alternatives typically occur \u2014 the training the Orders give mages to learn to use them is described in terms of basic athletic conditioning or fundamental mathematical principles, not side paths for One Weird Trick like Discipline ladders in Requiem.<br /> <br /> What do you want alternatives to the Order-specific Merits <i>for</i>, exactly? Like, &quot;custom magic styles&quot; is doing a lot of the heavy lifting in the conception of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:04:53-08:00","id":1503470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503464#post1503464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcanum Attainments aren't framed as something for which alternatives typically occur \u2014 the training the Orders give mages to learn to use them is described in terms of basic athletic conditioning or fundamental mathematical principles, not side paths for One Weird Trick like Discipline ladders in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it is just Utility attainments that are explained as <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Below are some of the most common Lesser Utilities, though the players and the Storyteller may devise others. </div> </div> </div>But whether Astral Adept, as an example, could be a utility attainment (considering it has great utility if you combine it with Summon Goetia)... I don't see a clear reason some things fit in one space (merits) rather than an other (Arcane attainments) - other than the variabke pre-requisites (like Fast Spells requires Time 1, i think).<br /> <br /> But regardless of the RAW, this is for a homebrew, trying to think through, if there was a fighting styles kind of 'skill tree' of merits - i suppose Astral Adept works just like a legacy attainment, in that it cannot be countered/affected by the lie...<br /> <br /> Imagining merits<br /> Thrown Spells -&gt; Fast Spells<br /> \\-&gt; Touch range in combat -&gt; Upgraded spell on striking with a weapon<br /> <br /> (Takes away the default ability to throw spells and to apply them by touching someone with the tip of your blade - but my players have never done either).<br /> <br /> Or High Speech -&gt; ???<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:11:10-08:00","id":1503471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503464#post1503464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you want alternatives to the Order-specific Merits <i>for</i>, exactly? Like, &quot;custom magic styles&quot; is doing a lot of the heavy lifting in the conception of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;style&quot; i do mean like 1e fighting styles.<br /> <br /> Having 'oh that is a combat spell casting style' - which anyone can learn, but is a series of merits allowing slight modifications to your spell casting (like the effect of Fast Spells).<br /> <br /> I think a Prime pre-requisited merit tree which starts with High Speech, and branches out to multiple uses probably already exists (possibly without the pre-req), plus everyone just gets Runes as a Yantra for free.<br /> <br /> Putting skills together in a tree all in the same place would have some minor advantage for players look through a list of 'magical styles' instead of them being scattered all over multiple books.<br /> <br /> But i am mainly thinking of how to add to these with ways to make casting magic feel distinct.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:25:24-08:00","id":1503476,"title":"","content":"You could use the system described in page 44 of <i>Hurt Locker</i>, which allow you to pick one maneuver out of many for each tier of a fighting style. Each style has a tag, so if you have enough dots in a style with a similar tag, you can buy a maneuver for one XP or even buy one of the alternative maneuvers in your current style.<br /> <br /> Which means that if you have 3 dots in Martial Arts, you have 3 maneuvers, one for each tier. So for one XP you could, for example, get another tier 3 maneuver, purchase the fourth dot or, since Boxing also has the Striking tag, you could purchase one Boxing maneuver up to tier 3. Which thematically it means studying mixed martial arts or retooling the technique to work within your main fighting system. The same can be done with supernatural styles, provided they share a tag and the character meets the minimum requirements of the other style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T13:07:19-08:00","id":1503482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503471#post1503471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By &quot;style&quot; i do mean like 1e fighting styles.<br /> <br /> Having 'oh that is a combat spell casting style' - which anyone can learn, but is a series of merits allowing slight modifications to your spell casting (like the effect of Fast Spells).<br /> <br /> I think a Prime pre-requisited merit tree which starts with High Speech, and branches out to multiple uses probably already exists (possibly without the pre-req), plus everyone just gets Runes as a Yantra for free.<br /> <br /> Putting skills together in a tree all in the same place would have some minor advantage for players look through a list of 'magical styles' instead of them being scattered all over multiple books.<br /> <br /> But i am mainly thinking of how to add to these with ways to make casting magic feel distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious what more you think could be done with magical combat style that a)Isn't covered by Adamant Hand, Between the Ticks and Fast Spells, b) accounts for the way combat in Chronicles works, c) Maintains the vibe of that <i>mainly</i> being the purview of the Adamantine Arrow, d) doesn't break the balances and feel of magic, and e) doesn't break the balance between magic and mundane violence in combat.<br /> <br /> Magic, in the context of combat, is intended to be something of a high risk, high reward scenario, something that's a viable action, but not strictly more viable than just cleaving a mother fucker or lighting them up with your SMG. Resources are neccesarily stretched thin for magic as a combat option, with Reach being limited to your own mastery or if it's a Rote and conventionally only being able to pull off a single Yantra, unless you decide to give up the sacred resource of time. It's not like diving into the thick of things and going slap happy like a spell-bender or Gandalf on a staff-happy day* is inviable given the touch option for spell casting, nor is slinging spells like Harrius Barius Potternicus took lessons from Vash the Stampede, particularly since every Mage has Mage Armor and spellcasting lets you make use of your Immediate Nimbus, but given that you can only do magic and use basic defense, it's not anymore encouraged than other combat options. This is on purpose, both to keep mundane physical combat viable and to keep magic apart as a special thing. Adamant Hand bridges the divide between the two by making it easier to transition between the two between turns with notable increases and permission for better defenses, all without neccesarily incentivizing one over the other.<br /> <br /> If you mean &quot;magical style&quot; in a non combat way (because you describe them like fighting styles but then make it about being distinctive from each other), the game already has that in Praxes, Rotes, Dedicated Tools, Shadow Names (and Cabal Themes), Legacies, Nimbus, and a lot more, all built on the foundation of Path and Order to help hone towards particularly distinctive styles. As Players go along, they're going to pick up a lot of things that will be signature to them-it's just something that takes work. It's not the sort of thing that you can hand players on a platter, it's something they have to curate, often with guidance and assistance from the Storyteller in the course of play.<br /> <br /> Magical Traditions, which is what I assumed you were going after with the magical styles, are a terrible mistake that the game has done a lot of work in running away from and is not benefitted from going back to. As for magical combat styles, I think my main comment on that is that I idly considered allowing a merit for being able to swing a punch or stab a motherfucker AND unleash a spell through it, and immediately realized that that would be broken as fuck.<br /> <br /> So, uh, yeah, I dislike flat out saying a homebrew is a bad idea, because often there's something interesting in them and they just happen to be poorly implemented, but this one. THis one feels like it's running straight into things that weren't good when we had them and won't be better now.<br /> <br /> *Not that staff-happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T15:11:57-08:00","id":1503494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503482#post1503482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious what more you think could be done with magical combat style that a)Isn't covered by Adamant Hand, Between the Ticks and Fast Spells, b) accounts for the way combat in Chronicles works, c) Maintains the vibe of that <i>mainly</i> being the purview of the Adamantine Arrow, d) doesn't break the balances and feel of magic, and e) doesn't break the balance between magic and mundane violence in combat.<br /> <br /> Magic, in the context of combat, is intended to be something of a high risk, high reward scenario, something that's a viable action, but not strictly more viable than just cleaving a mother fucker or lighting them up with your SMG. Resources are neccesarily stretched thin for magic as a combat option, with Reach being limited to your own mastery or if it's a Rote and conventionally only being able to pull off a single Yantra, unless you decide to give up the sacred resource of time. It's not like diving into the thick of things and going slap happy like a spell-bender or Gandalf on a staff-happy day* is inviable given the touch option for spell casting, nor is slinging spells like Harrius Barius Potternicus took lessons from Vash the Stampede, particularly since every Mage has Mage Armor and spellcasting lets you make use of your Immediate Nimbus, but given that you can only do magic and use basic defense, it's not anymore encouraged than other combat options. This is on purpose, both to keep mundane physical combat viable and to keep magic apart as a special thing. Adamant Hand bridges the divide between the two by making it easier to transition between the two between turns with notable increases and permission for better defenses, all without neccesarily incentivizing one over the other.<br /> <br /> If you mean &quot;magical style&quot; in a non combat way (because you describe them like fighting styles but then make it about being distinctive from each other), the game already has that in Praxes, Rotes, Dedicated Tools, Shadow Names (and Cabal Themes), Legacies, Nimbus, and a lot more, all built on the foundation of Path and Order to help hone towards particularly distinctive styles. As Players go along, they're going to pick up a lot of things that will be signature to them-it's just something that takes work. It's not the sort of thing that you can hand players on a platter, it's something they have to curate, often with guidance and assistance from the Storyteller in the course of play.<br /> <br /> Magical Traditions, which is what I assumed you were going after with the magical styles, are a terrible mistake that the game has done a lot of work in running away from and is not benefitted from going back to. As for magical combat styles, I think my main comment on that is that I idly considered allowing a merit for being able to swing a punch or stab a motherfucker AND unleash a spell through it, and immediately realized that that would be broken as fuck.<br /> <br /> So, uh, yeah, I dislike flat out saying a homebrew is a bad idea, because often there's something interesting in them and they just happen to be poorly implemented, but this one. THis one feels like it's running straight into things that weren't good when we had them and won't be better now.<br /> <br /> *Not that staff-happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback.<br /> <br /> Yeah, i was very much feeling like moving towards a more non-comvat way. Though i gave one example of a combat orientated style.<br /> <br /> The game has praxes, rotes and improvised spells. It has tools and Nimbuses, path and Order. But basically a Moros Mysterium can cast the same spells as a Thrysus Guardian, with the exception of Masques and Egregore.<br /> <br /> Now imagine a set of minor merits which are maybe a little less powerful than Masques or Egregore, but which anyone could learn.<br /> <br /> In the same sense that Fast spells and Between the Ticks are slightly less powerful than Adamant Hand. <br /> <br /> I think the problem in my head/my players heads, is it feels like some merits are things you buy at character creation rather than being things which can be taught/discovered.<br /> <br /> Like Dream or Destiny.... It feels like you can't learn how to have a destiny. But maybe that is a self-imposes limitation. Maybe Mages can learn to develop their destiny...<br /> <br /> But could you elaborate on what you mean by Traditions beinn a terrible idea (i am presuming this is a MtA reference). Why were they a terrible idea, and what about my idea is the same?<br /> <br /> Lastly, yeah, punch and unkeash a spell could be strong. I'm not sure how broken it would be, is you have to spend the mana, risk the paradox, and then is the punch misses you end up losing the spell? Might not be enough if a drawback to lessen how broken it is. Not too interested in the combat side of things tbh. But yeah, i should be careful with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T16:37:25-08:00","id":1503499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503494#post1503494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game has praxes, rotes and improvised spells. It has tools and Nimbuses, path and Order. But basically a Moros Mysterium can cast the same spells as a Thrysus Guardian, with the exception of Masques and Egregore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... yes and no? The effects those two hypothetical mages create may be the same, but their casting method will differ greatly, even if it's a Rote they have in common. Brandishing a lead-gilded (Lead, Moros) bible (Book, Mysterium) towards the target and staring the target down from behind a carved wooden (Wooden, Thyrsus) mask (Mask, Guardian) would be different ways to cast <u>Exorcism</u>, even if the spell itself is ultimately the same. I'm a bit hazy on Ascension mechanics, admittedly, but a Mage of any Tradition that sets someone on fire is ultimately casting &quot;ignite person&quot;, aren't they? The trappings are just different, which Yantras already do in Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503494#post1503494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now imagine a set of minor merits which are maybe a little less powerful than Masques or Egregore, but which anyone could learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those kinda already exist, at least in minor form. <i>Mana Sense</i>, <i>Fast Spells</i>, <i>Between Ticks</i>, <i>Prolifigate Dedication</i>, <i>Astral Adept</i>*, etc. They're good templates for one-trick abilities that encompass the Arcana, but aren't innate. I count <i>Dream</i> in that group, but I'll touch on it on one of your later points.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*<i>Astral Adept</i> as presented is, in my opinion, a Sleepwalker merit. The Awakened version would work better as costing the same as <i>Fast Spells</i> or <i>Mana Sense</i>, but requiring a dot of Mind. It's basically already a Mind merit like those two are Time and Prime merits respectively.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503494#post1503494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the same sense that Fast spells and Between the Ticks are slightly less powerful than Adamant Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're... not? <i>Fast Spells</i> is literally just learning to finger-gun your spells (or more seriously, to have good aim), which has applications outside of combat and can easily represent someone being very cautious with their Reach. <i>Between Ticks</i> <i>is</i> a more combat-focused ability, but whose functions arent really comprable to <i>Adamant Hand</i>'s &quot;make violence into a Yantra&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503494#post1503494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem in my head/my players heads, is it feels like some merits are things you buy at character creation rather than being things which can be taught/discovered.<br /> <br /> Like Dream or Destiny.... It feels like you can't learn how to have a destiny. But maybe that is a self-imposes limitation. Maybe Mages can learn to develop their destiny...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate Mages can throw <i>Destinies</i> on people, and arguably a Changeling could tamper enough with the skien of fate to inadvertently cause a change. The simplest in-game justification would be to have a Fate mage cast the relevant <i>Destiny</i> on the target over and over again until fate itself conforms to that design (i.e. the player buys the <i>Destiny</i> dots with XP). It's a bit less &quot;learn&quot; and a little more &quot;make/force&quot;, but the end result is the same.<br /> <br /> <i>Dream</i> likewise is pretty easy to justify learning in that anyone going into the Astral could handwave themselves learning and attuning to the currents of humanity's subconsious. Learn how to pick up on those pondrous cues, and you can start to sift out useful information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-19-2023, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T18:41:52-08:00","id":1503503,"title":"","content":"You could go to the Temenos Realm of Divinators and learn Dream from there. The mage could go through an occult training regiment using hallucinogens to teach them the right mindset to open themselves to reading the future. They could study the effects of reading a ouji board in different points of the Underworld, investigating what they point them towards and the insights they gain would build in their subconscious mind as the merit.<br /> <br /> Destiny can also be earned in character. They poked in one of the God Machine's Infrastructure and were marked by interacting with it or by its Angels as a person of interest, being integrated into its occult matrix. They developed a bond with a ghost, but part of the process for them to pass on involves taking on his karmic debt. They have a harrowing experience in an abandoned Sanctum of the Geryon Ministry and wake up with a Destiny.\u200b<br /> <br /> Destinies are a double edged sword, you become able to achieve greatness, but risk being mentally, emotionally or spiritually broken as well. Purely positive ones are the purview of Fate masters. So in general they are something you stumble into rather than actively seek, with the exception of negotiating with a Fate Supernal summon for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-20-2023, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T18:46:21-08:00","id":1503504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503494#post1503494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But could you elaborate on what you mean by Traditions beinn a terrible idea (i am presuming this is a MtA reference). Why were they a terrible idea, and what about my idea is the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason &quot;your magic benefits from your engagement with an established real-world cultural magical tradition&quot; is just part of Techn\u00e9: as a general phenomenon, insight into things that resonate with Supernal Truth is not unique to occult traditions; symbolism can be found and drawn upon from anything, which is why Techn\u00e9 affords the same benefits to computer networking and knitting and why the Diamond just focuses on developing their own mythology and practices.<br /> <br /> There's a comparison to be made with Deviant here: Awakened spellcasting is an incredibly versatile system where each spell can be made to work differently in terms of where it gets its bonuses from, and belonging to a major occult conspiracy or adhering to a focused magical philosophy can give you some additional tricks, but none of that is going to fix the fundamental problem you have of &quot;two characters from different traditions use the same basic systems for magic that accomplishes the same result with the same Arcana.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of this is down to Mage not having the space to really emphasize improvised casting as being more difficult than using Rotes or Praxes, but if you want an example of something off-the-cuff, you could do something like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841832-homebrew-changeling-merits?p=1497688#post1497688\">this thing I did for changelings personalizing their Contracts</a> and build a set of Merits whose prerequisites are knowledge of a specific spell as a Praxis (or a Rote, depending on what you want the Merit to represent). Again: custom Merits are pretty much the path of least resistance for building this sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T19:05:56-08:00","id":1503505,"title":"","content":"There's also the factor of &quot;if you have a special paradigm that is meaningfully distinct from others, then you have a tool everyone is going to use over the standard system, at which point there's no point to the standard system.&quot; The M:tAw sourcebook Magical Traditions, the nearest mirror to this concept, didn't make sense for the &quot;symbolism in everything&quot; magical jackdaw style of Awakening and mechanically injured gameplay by having players who weren't using it be left behind so bad it basically had to be hard disawoved from the canon in the buildup to Second Edition's release. Fortunately, we're now at a point where no one really mentions it, and what good was in their concept being appropriately spread across the order mechanics, with the most superficial benefits going to Techne, and the Nameless Order Merit and Legacies that are particularly devoted to it.<br /> <br /> Players can develop their own individual style, and there are benefits of empowerment to do so baked into the game, but it falls on them to build it up, and part of that is understanding the tools they have to make that work. That's, in fact, a big part of the narrative, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887107-understand-wisdom?p=895967#post895967\">each mage making their own face</a>. I wouldn't short cut that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-19-2023, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T19:29:32-08:00","id":1503506,"title":"","content":"Also, Dave Brookshaw's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/8717-are-traditions-going-to-be-ignored-or-embraced-in-the-future-of-the-gameline?p=14013#post14013\">old thought on the subject</a>.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T20:07:06-08:00","id":1503507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503503#post1503503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could go to the Temenos Realm of Divinators and learn Dream from there. The mage could go through an occult training regiment using to teach them the right mindset to open themselves to reading the future. They could study the effects of reading a ouji board in different points of the Underworld, investing what they point them towards and the insights would build in their subconscious mind as the merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont let your Dreams be memes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments#post1503456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something i was reading about a 1.5e homebrew got me thinking about custom magic 'styles' which could be added (or removed) from the game.<br /> <br /> Throw spell could have been a supernatural merit, and a pre-requisite for fast spells.<br /> <br /> Counter spell, likewise<br /> <br /> Or a Highspeech, Runic writing, Second Person High Speech, Invisible runes series of merits...<br /> <br /> I'd like some alternatives to the Order specific merits. Maybe an Oneiromacy series starting with Astral Adept?<br /> <br /> What are the relevant advantages of custom merits over custom Arcane attainments/alternative utility attainments? / Legacies?<br /> <br /> I think i want something like a set of minor legacy 'skill trees' which don't lock you out of other learning (With or without Arcana pre-reqs)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> There's also something to be said for not creating out-and-out skill/feat trees. Gnosis-Arcana, Style merits, and the Advanced Library/Sanctum/Safe Place Merits are the closest we really get to skill-trees, and that last one is already kinda stretching my tolerance for that DnD-esque mechanic.<br /> <br /> Not everything fits into nice linear progressions - I can read Japanese and Chinese infinitely better than I can speak them, for example, but I know plenty of people for whom the reverse is true. But TTRPGs often assume that if you have competence in one form of communication, you also have the other. The Highspeech --&gt; Runic writing --&gt; Second Person High Speech --&gt; Invisible Runes chain would fall into that trap of assumed omni-competence. You <i>could</i> set it up as a bunch of branches off of High Speech, but that's rather cumbersome, risks becoming an Exalted-Charms-esque mess, and ultimately detracts from usability rather than adds variety.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Not to say you can't make more Utility-Attainment-esque merits, there's definately a place for them. Just that I personally don't think their requirements should exceed a few dots in the relevant Arcana and Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-20-2023, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T02:36:41-08:00","id":1503516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503456-home-brew-merits-vs-arcane-attainments?p=1503506#post1503506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Dave Brookshaw's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/8717-are-traditions-going-to-be-ignored-or-embraced-in-the-future-of-the-gameline?p=14013#post14013\">old thought on the subject</a>.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sleeper/real world magical styles are not what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> I am imaging a set of skills the orders can teach (like high speech), but optionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}